# CLAUDE.md — tests

**Tests are end to end or not at all** (root `CLAUDE.md`). No unit or component tests, no tier ladder, no fail-first
ritual, nothing in `tests/Unit` or `tests/Feature`.
<!-- if:spa -->
Browser flows live in `frontend/e2e/` under the same rule (Browser flows, below).
<!-- endif -->

## What is written

Only E2E tests, in `tests/E2E/`: one whole flow per test through its real entry point (an HTTP request through
routing, middleware, controller and database; an artisan command), asserting what a person or operator sees:
<!-- if:htmx -->
the page, the flash, the payload, the records left behind.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:htmx -->
the status, the payload, the headers, the records left behind.
<!-- endif -->
Behaviour-named (`it('…')`), `uses(RefreshDatabase::class)`.

- Seed the world with the factories; drive it through the entry point, never by calling a service, model or job.
- Auth state comes through its route: `actingAs($user)` for a signed-in user, `POST route('password.confirm.store')`
  for a confirmation. Never `withSession([...])` to forge a gate's state (`auth.password_confirmed_at`, `login.id`, a
  stored OAuth flow).
- Reference data is already there: `TestCase` carries `#[Seeder(ReferenceDataSeeder::class)]` (once per process).
  Look reference rows up by slug; never factory them.
- Fake only what is paid or outside; nothing of our own code:
  - LLM calls: the SDK's fakes.
  - Outbound HTTP: `Http::fake` + `Http::preventStrayRequests()`.
  - Mail: the `array` mailer (`phpunit.xml`) keeps what was sent.
  - OAuth providers: `Socialite::fake('<provider>', Two\User::fake([...]))`, with `services.<provider>` `client_id`,
    `client_secret` and `redirect` set in the test (the fake forwards `with()` and `scopes()` to the real driver) and
    the provider on via `config(['services.socialite.providers' => [...]])`.
- Queues run inline (`QUEUE_CONNECTION=sync` in `phpunit.xml`), so a chain or queued job runs for real in the flow.
- Machine addresses come from the environment (e.g. the host of `LOCAL_APP_URL`), never a literal; stand-ins are RFC
  5737 (`192.0.2.x`, `198.51.100.x`, `203.0.113.x`).
- Run only the E2E test you wrote or touched: `php artisan test --compact tests/E2E/…`. The full run belongs to
  review and to the owner before a push, never to a commit.

## Auth proofs

Each is an E2E flow, written when the piece it proves is built.

- Every write flow's denial test posts an invalid body as a user without access and asserts 403 (or 404), never 422:
  authorization runs before validation (`app/Http/Controllers/CLAUDE.md`).
- Fortify: its routes and the two-factor flow, proved by the auth tests setup ships in `tests/E2E/`.
<!-- if:htmx -->
<!-- unless:auth-pages -->
  The views flip rewrites the route test (`resources/CLAUDE.md`, Auth pages).
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:auth-pages -->
  The route test proves the views on: the GET pages answer 200, and the JSON flows send `Accept: application/json`.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- endif -->
- Social sign-in:
  - a vouched new user is created with a null password, linked and signed in, and the session id changes;
  - an unvouched provider email creates no user and no link until the mailed link is opened in the same session;
    opened in another session it creates nothing; an email collision is refused (guest, no row);
  - a returning user signs in by `provider_user_id`;
<!-- if:htmx -->
  - linking while signed in is a POST and needs confirmation: unconfirmed, it redirects to the confirm page;
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:htmx -->
  - linking while signed in needs confirmation: a plain POST without `Accept: application/json` answers 423, not a
    redirect;
<!-- endif -->
  - a link callback after the session user changed, or with no stored flow, is refused;
  - an account linked to another user is refused, and unlinking the last way in is refused;
  - a user with confirmed 2FA is sent to the challenge, not signed in;
  - an unknown or disabled provider is a 404;
  - a passwordless user cannot confirm with an empty password.
- Sanctum:
<!-- unless:tenancy -->
  - a token from `createToken` reaches an `auth:sanctum` route; no token gets a 401 JSON answer;
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:tenancy -->
  - a token from `User::createTenantToken` reaches an `auth:sanctum` route; no token gets a 401 JSON answer;
<!-- endif -->
<!-- if:spa -->
  - the session-cookie path is proven by the Playwright session flow (below), not by Pest: a Pest test's session store
    keeps its attributes across requests, so it never exercises the stateful match.
<!-- endif -->
<!-- unless:spa -->
  - `actingAs($user)`, then `getJson` on an `/api/v1` route, is 401 (`sanctum.guard` is empty).
<!-- endif -->
